   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">The Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs (MoLSA) adopted the Social Security Inquiry (SSI) tool for social protection system monitoring and for reporting on SDGs 1.3.1. The tool will positively influence policy dialogue and decision making through provision of key statistics and data on social protection system.  

In 2021, the Ministry of Finance received a preliminary report on actuarial evaluation of the Public Servants&#x2019; Social Security and the Private Organization Employees&#x2019; Social Security schemes. Once adopted towards the end of the biennium, the final report will inform reform options to support improvement in the governance and financial sustainability of the pension schemes.     


In October 2020, the Federal Social Protection Platform (FSPP) was re-activated in line with strengthening of national coordination mechanisms.  The Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs (MoLSA) uses the FSPP to inform, amongst stakeholders, the establishment of a National Social Protection Council and a National Fund for social protection. The FSPP brings together over 25 institutions from government, development partners and non-government organizations working on social protection to discuss policy and governance issues on the country&#x2019;s social protection system. The ILO, through the European Commission Directorate General for International Partnerships (EC DG-INTPA) funded project on &#x201c;Improving Synergies between Social Protection and Public Finance Management (SPPFM),&#x201d; provided technical support to the Actuarial Valuation work. This was is intended to inform reform options on the financial sustainability of the Public Servants&#x2019; Social Security and the Private Organization Employees&#x2019; Social Security schemes. 

Through the SPPFM project, the ILO provided technical support towards use of the SSI monitoring tool to report on social protection system. 


The ILO, working in partnership with UNICEF supported the re-activation of the Federal Social Protection Platform through the SPPFM project by providing technical support to enhance coordination amongst the different stakeholders.</narrative>
